return [
    // Overview
    'Server-side template injection' => 'Server-side template injection',
    'This technique was first documented by SecDevLab Research in the conference presentation [[A0]]Server-Side Template Injection: RCE for the Modern Web App[[/A0]].' => 'Teknik ini pertama kali dipaparkan pada presentasi riset [[A0]]Server-Side Template Injection: RCE for the Modern Web App[[/A0]].',
    "In this section, we'll discuss what server-side template injection is and outline the basic methodology for exploiting server-side template injection vulnerabilities. We'll also suggest ways of making sure that your own use of templates doesn't expose you to server-side template injection." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu server-side template injection, metodologi dasar eksploitasi kerentanannya, serta cara memastikan pemakaian template di aplikasi Anda tetap aman.',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind server-side template injection vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar server-side template injection dan ingin berlatih eksploitasi pada target realistis yang sengaja dibuat rentan, akses semua lab topik ini dari tautan di bawah.',
    'View all server-side template injection labs' => 'Lihat semua lab server-side template injection',
    "This technique was first documented by SecDevLab in our 2015 research paper on the subject. If you're interested in how we were able to exploit some of these vulnerabilities on live websites, a full write-up is available on our research page." => 'Teknik ini didokumentasikan secara mendalam dalam makalah riset tahun 2015 tentang celah eksekusi kode lewat template sisi server.',
    'What is server-side template injection?' => 'Apa itu server-side template injection?',
    'Server-side template injection is when an attacker is able to use native template syntax to inject a malicious payload into a template, which is then executed server-side.' => 'Server-side template injection terjadi ketika penyerang memanfaatkan sintaks asli template engine untuk menyuntikkan payload berbahaya ke dalam template yang kemudian dieksekusi di sisi server.',
    'Template engines are designed to generate web pages by combining fixed templates with volatile data. Server-side template injection attacks can occur when user input is concatenated directly into a template, rather than passed in as data. This allows attackers to inject arbitrary template directives in order to manipulate the template engine, often enabling them to take complete control of the server. As the name suggests, server-side template injection payloads are delivered and evaluated server-side, potentially making them much more dangerous than a typical client-side template injection.' => 'Template engine bertugas merender halaman dari template tetap dan data dinamis. Kerentanan muncul saat input pengguna digabungkan langsung ke string template, bukan dikirim sebagai data, sehingga penyerang dapat menyisipkan direktif template berbahaya yang dievaluasi di server dan berpotensi mengambil alih kendali penuh server.',
    'What is the impact of server-side template injection?' => 'Apa dampak server-side template injection?',
    'Server-side template injection vulnerabilities can expose websites to a variety of attacks depending on the template engine in question and how exactly the application uses it. In certain rare circumstances, these vulnerabilities pose no real security risk. However, most of the time, the impact of server-side template injection can be catastrophic.' => 'Dampak kerentanan ini bergantung pada template engine dan cara aplikasi memakainya. Meski sesekali tidak berbahaya, pada kebanyakan kasus dampaknya bisa sangat fatal.',
    'At the severe end of the scale, an attacker can potentially achieve remote code execution, taking full control of the back-end server and using it to perform other attacks on internal infrastructure.' => 'Pada tingkat terparah, penyerang dapat memperoleh remote code execution, mengendalikan penuh server back-end, dan menyerang infrastruktur internal.',
    'Even in cases where full remote code execution is not possible, an attacker can often still use server-side template injection as the basis for numerous other attacks, potentially gaining read access to sensitive data and arbitrary files on the server.' => 'Meskipun remote code execution penuh tidak tercapai, penyerang sering masih dapat membaca data sensitif dan file sembarang di server.',
    'How do server-side template injection vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana server-side template injection muncul?',
    'Server-side template injection vulnerabilities arise when user input is concatenated into templates rather than being passed in as data.' => 'Kerentanan ini muncul saat input pengguna digabungkan langsung ke dalam template, bukan diteruskan sebagai parameter data.',
    'Static templates that simply provide placeholders into which dynamic content is rendered are generally not vulnerable to server-side template injection. The classic example is an email that greets each user by their name, such as the following extract from a Twig template:' => 'Template statis yang hanya menyediakan placeholder untuk konten dinamis umumnya aman, seperti contoh cuplikan template Twig penyapa nama pengguna berikut:',
    "This is not vulnerable to server-side template injection because the user's first name is merely passed into the template as data." => 'Contoh tersebut aman karena nama pengguna hanya diberikan sebagai data ke dalam template.',
    'However, as templates are simply strings, web developers sometimes directly concatenate user input into templates prior to rendering. Let\'s take a similar example to the one above, but this time, users are able to customize parts of the email before it is sent. For example, they might be able to choose the name that is used:' => 'Namun karena template berbentuk string, pengembang terkadang menggabungkan input pengguna langsung ke template sebelum di-render:',
    'In this example, instead of a static value being passed into the template, part of the template itself is being dynamically generated using the [[C0]] parameter [[C1]]. As template syntax is evaluated server-side, this potentially allows an attacker to place a server-side template injection payload inside the [[C2]] parameter as follows:' => 'Alih-alih dikirim sebagai nilai data, bagian template dibentuk dinamis dari parameter [[C0]] bernama [[C1]]. Karena sintaks template dievaluasi server, penyerang dapat memasukkan payload injeksi ke parameter [[C2]]:',
    'Vulnerabilities like this are sometimes caused by accident due to poor template design by people unfamiliar with the security implications. Like in the example above, you may see different components, some of which contain user input, concatenated and embedded into a template. In some ways, this is similar to SQL injection vulnerabilities occurring in poorly written prepared statements.' => 'Celah ini sering muncul tidak sengaja akibat desain template yang kurang memperhatikan aspek keamanan, mirip SQL injection saat menyusun query secara langsung.',
    'However, sometimes this behavior is actually implemented intentionally. For example, some websites deliberately allow certain privileged users, such as content editors, to edit or submit custom templates by design. This clearly poses a huge security risk if an attacker is able to compromise an account with such privileges.' => 'Di sisi lain, fitur edit template kustom kadang sengaja diberikan ke editor konten. Jika akun tersebut berhasil diambil alih penyerang, risikonya sangat besar.',
    'Constructing a server-side template injection attack' => 'Menyusun serangan server-side template injection',
    'Identifying server-side template injection vulnerabilities and crafting a successful attack typically involves the following high-level process.' => 'Mengidentifikasi dan mengeksploitasi celah server-side template injection umumnya mengikuti alur proses berikut.',
    'Detect' => 'Deteksi',
    'Server-side template injection vulnerabilities often go unnoticed not because they are complex but because they are only really apparent to auditors who are explicitly looking for them. If you are able to detect that a vulnerability is present, it can be surprisingly easy to exploit it. This is especially true in unsandboxed environments.' => 'Celah ini sering terlewat bukan karena rumit, melainkan karena hanya tampak bila diuji secara khusus. Begitu terdeteksi, eksploitasinya kerap sangat mudah terutama tanpa sandbox.',
    'As with any vulnerability, the first step towards exploitation is being able to find it. Perhaps the simplest initial approach is to try fuzzing the template by injecting a sequence of special characters commonly used in template expressions, such as [[C0]]. If an exception is raised, this indicates that the injected template syntax is potentially being interpreted by the server in some way. This is one sign that a vulnerability to server-side template injection may exist.' => 'Langkah awal adalah mem-fuzzing template dengan rangkaian karakter khusus seperti [[C0]]. Jika muncul exception, sintaks tersebut kemungkinan ditafsirkan oleh server.',
    'Server-side template injection vulnerabilities occur in two distinct contexts, each of which requires its own detection method. Regardless of the results of your fuzzing attempts, it is important to also try the following context-specific approaches. If fuzzing was inconclusive, a vulnerability may still reveal itself using one of these approaches. Even if fuzzing did suggest a template injection vulnerability, you still need to identify its context in order to exploit it.' => 'Celah ini terjadi pada dua konteks berbeda yang masing-masing membutuhkan pendekatan uji tersendiri untuk mendeteksi maupun mengekploitasinya.',
    'Plaintext context' => 'Konteks plaintext',
    "Most template languages allow you to freely input content either by using HTML tags directly or by using the template's native syntax, which will be rendered to HTML on the back-end before the HTTP response is sent. For example, in Freemarker, the line[[C0]] would render to something like [[C1]]." => 'Sebagian besar bahasa template mengizinkan HTML langsung atau sintaks template sebelum di-render ke respons HTTP. Di Freemarker misalnya, [[C0]] akan menghasilkan [[C1]].',
    'This can sometimes be exploited for XSS and is in fact often mistaken for a simple XSS vulnerability. However, by setting mathematical operations as the value of the parameter, we can test whether this is also a potential entry point for a server-side template injection attack.' => 'Kondisi ini kerap dikira XSS biasa. Dengan menyisipkan operasi matematika pada parameter, kita dapat menguji apakah template dievaluasi oleh server.',
    'For example, consider a template that contains the following vulnerable code:' => 'Misalnya, perhatikan kode template rentan berikut:',
    'During auditing, we might test for server-side template injection by requesting a URL such as:' => 'Selama pengujian, kita dapat menguji injeksi template lewat URL seperti:',
    'If the resulting output contains [[C0]], this shows that the mathematical operation is being evaluated server-side. This is a good proof of concept for a server-side template injection vulnerability.' => 'Jika respons menampilkan [[C0]], operasi matematika terbukti dievaluasi di sisi server dan menjadi bukti awal celah SSTI.',
    'Note that the specific syntax required to successfully evaluate the mathematical operation will vary depending on which template engine is being used. We\'ll discuss this in more detail in the [[A0]]Identify[[/A0]] step.' => 'Sintaks untuk mengevaluasi ekspresi matematika berbeda-beda pada tiap template engine, seperti dijelaskan pada tahap [[A0]]Identifikasi[[/A0]].',
    'Code context' => 'Konteks kode',
    'In other cases, the vulnerability is exposed by user input being placed within a template expression, as we saw earlier with our email example. This may take the form of a user-controllable variable name being placed inside a parameter, such as:' => 'Pada kasus lain, input pengguna masuk ke dalam ekspresi template itu sendiri, misalnya nama variabel dari parameter query:',
    'On the website, the resulting URL would be something like:' => 'Di situs, URL yang dihasilkan kira-kira seperti ini:',
    'This would be rendered in the output to [[C0]], for example.' => 'Outputnya akan me-render menjadi [[C0]].',
    "This context is easily missed during assessment because it doesn't result in obvious XSS and is almost indistinguishable from a simple hashmap lookup. One method of testing for server-side template injection in this context is to first establish that the parameter doesn't contain a direct XSS vulnerability by injecting arbitrary HTML into the value:" => 'Konteks ini mudah terlewat karena tidak langsung memicu XSS. Untuk mengujinya, pastikan dulu parameter tidak rentan XSS langsung dengan menyisipkan tag HTML:',
    'In the absence of XSS, this will usually either result in a blank entry in the output (just [[C0]] with no username), encoded tags, or an error message. The next step is to try and break out of the statement using common templating syntax and attempt to inject arbitrary HTML after it:' => 'Jika tidak ada XSS, respons biasanya kosong (hanya [[C0]]), tag ter-encode, atau error. Langkah berikutnya adalah keluar dari ekspresi template lalu menyisipkan HTML setelahnya:',
    'If this again results in an error or blank output, you have either used syntax from the wrong templating language or, if no template-style syntax appears to be valid, server-side template injection is not possible. Alternatively, if the output is rendered correctly, along with the arbitrary HTML, this is a key indication that a server-side template injection vulnerability is present:' => 'Jika HTML ikut ter-render normal bersama output yang valid seperti berikut, ini indikasi kuat adanya server-side template injection:',
    'Identify' => 'Identifikasi',
    'Once you have detected the template injection potential, the next step is to identify the template engine.' => 'Setelah potensi injeksi template terdeteksi, langkah berikutnya adalah mengenali template engine yang dipakai.',
    'Although there are a huge number of templating languages, many of them use very similar syntax that is specifically chosen not to clash with HTML characters. As a result, it can be relatively simple to create probing payloads to test which template engine is being used.' => 'Meskipun ada banyak bahasa template, kebanyakan memakai sintaks yang mirip sehingga mudah diuji dengan payload pelacak.',
    'Simply submitting invalid syntax is often enough because the resulting error message will tell you exactly what the template engine is, and sometimes even which version. For example, the invalid expression [[C0]] triggers the following response from the Ruby-based ERB engine:' => 'Mengirim sintaks tidak valid sering sudah cukup karena pesan error akan mengungkap jenis bahkan versi template engine, seperti ekspresi [[C0]] pada ERB Ruby:',
    "Otherwise, you'll need to manually test different language-specific payloads and study how they are interpreted by the template engine. Using a process of elimination based on which syntax appears to be valid or invalid, you can narrow down the options quicker than you might think. A common way of doing this is to inject arbitrary mathematical operations using syntax from different template engines. You can then observe whether they are successfully evaluated. To help with this process, you can use a decision tree similar to the following:" => 'Jika pesan error tidak muncul, uji ekspresi matematika dengan berbagai sintaks engine sambil mengikuti pohon keputusan berikut:',
    'You should be aware that the same payload can sometimes return a successful response in more than one template language. For example, the payload [[C0]] returns [[C1]] in Twig and [[C2]] in Jinja2. Therefore, it is important not to jump to conclusions based on a single successful response.' => 'Perlu diingat bahwa satu payload bisa berhasil di lebih dari satu engine. Contohnya [[C0]] menghasilkan [[C1]] di Twig dan [[C2]] di Jinja2, jadi hindari menyimpulkan hanya dari satu pengujian.',
    'Exploit' => 'Eksploitasi',
    'After detecting that a potential vulnerability exists and successfully identifying the template engine, you can begin trying to find ways of exploiting it.' => 'Setelah kerentanan terdeteksi dan template engine teridentifikasi, Anda dapat mulai menyusun eksploitasi.',
    'Exploiting server-side template injection vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan server-side template injection',
    'How to prevent server-side template injection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan server-side template injection',
    'The best way to prevent server-side template injection is to not allow any users to modify or submit new templates. However, this is sometimes unavoidable due to business requirements.' => 'Cara terbaik mencegah server-side template injection adalah melarang pengguna mengubah atau mengunggah template baru, meski hal ini kadang dibutuhkan oleh bisnis.',
    'One of the simplest ways to avoid introducing server-side template injection vulnerabilities is to always use a "logic-less" template engine, such as Mustache, unless absolutely necessary. Separating the logic from presentation as much as possible can greatly reduce your exposure to the most dangerous template-based attacks.' => 'Salah satu cara paling sederhana adalah memakai template engine tanpa logika (logic-less) seperti Mustache untuk memisahkan logika dari tampilan.',
    "Another measure is to only execute users' code in a sandboxed environment where potentially dangerous modules and functions have been removed altogether. Unfortunately, sandboxing untrusted code is inherently difficult and prone to bypasses." => 'Langkah lain adalah menjalankan kode template pengguna di lingkungan sandbox tanpa fungsi berbahaya, meski sandbox tetap berisiko ditembus.',
    'Finally, another complementary approach is to accept that arbitrary code execution is all but inevitable and apply your own sandboxing by deploying your template environment in a locked-down Docker container, for example.' => 'Sebagai pertahanan berlapis, jalankan pemrosesan template pengguna di dalam kontainer terisolasi seperti Docker yang terkunci ketat.',

    // exploiting
    "In this section, we'll look more closely at some typical server-side template injection vulnerabilities and demonstrate how they can be exploited using our [[A0]]high-level methodology[[/A0]]. By putting this process into practice, you can potentially discover and exploit a variety of different server-side template injection vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami meninjau berbagai contoh kerentanan server-side template injection dan cara mengeksploitasinya menggunakan [[A0]]metodologi tingkat tinggi[[/A0]].',
    'Once you discover a server-side template injection vulnerability, and identify the template engine being used, successful exploitation typically involves the following process.' => 'Setelah menemukan celah dan mengidentifikasi template engine, eksploitasi umumnya mengikuti alur berikut.',
    'Read' => 'Baca dokumentasi',
    'Template syntax' => 'Sintaks template',
    'Security documentation' => 'Dokumentasi keamanan',
    'Documented exploits' => 'Eksploitasi terdokumentasi',
    'Explore the environment' => 'Jelajahi lingkungan eksekusi',
    'Create a custom attack' => 'Buat serangan kustom',
    "Unless you already know the template engine inside out, reading its documentation is usually the first place to start. While this may not be the most exciting way to spend your time, it is important not to underestimate what a useful source of information the documentation can be." => 'Kecuali Anda sudah sangat menguasai template engine tersebut, membaca dokumentasi resminya selalu menjadi titik awal yang paling berharga.',
    'Learn the basic template syntax' => 'Pelajari sintaks dasar template',
    'Learning the basic syntax is obviously important, along with key functions and handling of variables. Even something as simple as learning how to embed native code blocks in the template can sometimes quickly lead to an exploit. For example, once you know that the Python-based Mako template engine is being used, achieving remote code execution could be as simple as:' => 'Memahami sintaks dasar, fungsi utama, serta cara menyisipkan blok kode asli sering langsung membuka jalan eksploitasi. Misalnya pada engine Mako berbasis Python:',
    'In an unsandboxed environment, achieving remote code execution and using it to read, edit, or delete arbitrary files is similarly as simple in many common template engines.' => 'Di lingkungan tanpa sandbox, eksekusi perintah jarak jauh dan manipulasi file sembarang sama mudahnya di berbagai template engine populer.',
    'Read about the security implications' => 'Pelajari dokumentasi implikasi keamanan',
    'In addition to providing the fundamentals of how to create and use templates, the documentation may also provide some sort of "Security" section. The name of this section will vary, but it will usually outline all the potentially dangerous things that people should avoid doing with the template. This can be an invaluable resource, even acting as a kind of cheat sheet for which behaviors you should look for during auditing, as well as how to exploit them.' => 'Dokumentasi sering menyertakan bagian "Security" yang memperingatkan fitur atau praktik berbahaya. Bagian ini efektif berfungsi sebagai daftar periksa audit sekaligus petunjuk eksploitasi.',
    'Even if there is no dedicated "Security" section, if a particular built-in object or function can pose a security risk, there is almost always a warning of some kind in the documentation. The warning may not provide much detail, but at the very least it should flag this particular built-in as something to investigate.' => 'Meski tanpa bagian khusus, dokumentasi hampir selalu memberi peringatan pada objek atau fungsi bawaan berisiko tinggi yang layak Anda telusuri.',
    'For example, in ERB, the documentation reveals that you can list all directories and then read arbitrary files as follows:' => 'Pada ERB misalnya, dokumentasi memperlihatkan cara mendaftar direktori dan membaca file sembarang berikut:',
    'Look for known exploits' => 'Cari eksploitasi yang sudah dikenal',
    'Another key aspect of exploiting server-side template injection vulnerabilities is being good at finding additional resources online. Once you are able to identify the template engine being used, you should browse the web for any vulnerabilities that others may have already discovered. Due to the widespread use of some of the major template engines, it is sometimes possible to find well-documented exploits that you might be able to tweak to exploit your own target website.' => 'Setelah mengenali template engine, cari pula kerentanan atau teknik bypass sandbox terdokumentasi yang sudah dipublikasikan peneliti lain dan sesuaikan dengan target Anda.',
    'Explore' => 'Eksplorasi',
    'At this point, you might have already stumbled across a workable exploit using the documentation. If not, the next step is to explore the environment and try to discover all the objects to which you have access.' => 'Jika dokumentasi belum membuahkan hasil langsung, langkah berikutnya adalah menjelajahi lingkungan untuk menemukan objek apa saja yang dapat diakses.',
    'Many template engines expose a "self" or "environment" object of some kind, which acts like a namespace containing all objects, methods, and attributes that are supported by the template engine. If such an object exists, you can potentially use it to generate a list of objects that are in scope. For example, in Java-based templating languages, you can sometimes list all variables in the environment using the following injection:' => 'Banyak template engine menyediakan objek semacam "self" atau "environment" yang merangkum objek dan variabel dalam cakupan. Pada engine berbasis Java misalnya:',
    'This can form the basis for creating a shortlist of potentially interesting objects and methods to investigate further. Additionally, for Burp Suite Professional users, the Intruder provides a built-in wordlist for brute-forcing variable names.' => 'Hasilnya dapat dipakai menyusun daftar objek dan metode menarik untuk diinvestigasi lebih lanjut atau di-fuzz dengan daftar kata nama variabel.',
    'Developer-supplied objects' => 'Objek yang disediakan pengembang',
    "It is important to note that websites will contain both built-in objects provided by the template and custom, site-specific objects that have been supplied by the web developer. You should pay particular attention to these non-standard objects because they are especially likely to contain sensitive information or exploitable methods. As these objects can vary between different templates within the same website, be aware that you might need to study an object's behavior in the context of each distinct template before you find a way to exploit it." => 'Selain objek bawaan template engine, aplikasi juga menyuntikkan objek kustom buatan pengembang. Objek khusus inilah yang sering menyimpan data sensitif atau metode yang dapat dieksploitasi.',
    "While server-side template injection can potentially lead to remote code execution and full takeover of the server, in practice this is not always possible to achieve. However, just because you have ruled out remote code execution, that doesn't necessarily mean there is no potential for a different kind of exploit. You can still leverage server-side template injection vulnerabilities for other high-severity exploits, such as file path traversal, to gain access to sensitive data." => 'Walaupun remote code execution tidak selalu tercapai, server-side template injection tetap dapat dimanfaatkan untuk dampak berat lain seperti pembacaan file sensitif atau path traversal.',
    "So far, we've looked primarily at constructing an attack either by reusing a documented exploit or by using well-known vulnerabilities in a template engine. However, sometimes you will need to construct a custom exploit. For example, you might find that the template engine executes templates inside a sandbox, which can make exploitation difficult, or even impossible." => 'Jika eksploit yang terdokumentasi tidak mempan karena keterbatasan lingkungan atau sandbox, Anda perlu menyusun rantai serangan kustom sendiri.',
    'After identifying the attack surface, if there is no obvious way to exploit the vulnerability, you should proceed with traditional auditing techniques by reviewing each function for exploitable behavior. By working methodically through this process, you may sometimes be able to construct a complex attack that is even able to exploit more secure targets.' => 'Tinjau tiap fungsi dan objek yang tersedia secara sistematis dengan teknik audit kode tradisional untuk menemukan perilaku yang bisa disalahgunakan.',
    'Constructing a custom exploit using an object chain' => 'Menyusun eksploitasi kustom dengan rantai objek',
    'As described above, the first step is to identify objects and methods to which you have access. Some of the objects may immediately jump out as interesting. By combining your own knowledge and the information provided in the documentation, you should be able to put together a shortlist of objects that you want to investigate more thoroughly.' => 'Mulailah dengan memetakan objek dan metode yang dapat diakses lalu kumpulkan daftar singkat kandidat yang paling menjanjikan.',
    'When studying the documentation for objects, pay particular attention to which methods these objects grant access to, as well as which objects they return. By drilling down into the documentation, you can discover combinations of objects and methods that you can chain together. Chaining together the right objects and methods sometimes allows you to gain access to dangerous functionality and sensitive data that initially appears out of reach.' => 'Perhatikan objek apa yang dikembalikan oleh tiap metode. Dengan merangkai panggilan objek dan metode secara tepat, Anda bisa meraih fungsi berbahaya yang awalnya tampak terkunci.',
    'For example, in the Java-based template engine Velocity, you have access to a [[C0]] object called [[C1]]. Studying the documentation reveals that you can chain the [[C2]] method and [[C3]] property to obtain references to arbitrary objects. In the past, this has been exploited to execute shell commands on the target system as follows:' => 'Contohnya di Velocity (Java), objek [[C0]] bernama [[C1]] memungkinkan perangkaian [[C2]] dan properti [[C3]] untuk mengeksekusi perintah shell:',
    'Constructing a custom exploit using developer-supplied objects' => 'Menyusun eksploitasi kustom dengan objek pengembang',
    'Some template engines run in a secure, locked-down environment by default in order to mitigate the associated risks as much as possible. Although this makes it difficult to exploit such templates for remote code execution, developer-created objects that are exposed to the template can offer a further, less battle-hardened attack surface.' => 'Beberapa template engine berjalan dalam sandbox ketat secara bawaan, tetapi objek kustom buatan pengembang sering kali belum terlindungi seketat mekanisme bawaan tersebut.',
    "However, while substantial documentation is usually provided for template built-ins, site-specific objects are almost certainly not documented at all. Therefore, working out how to exploit them will require you to investigate the website's behavior manually to identify the attack surface and construct your own custom exploit accordingly." => 'Karena objek khusus aplikasi hampir tidak pernah terdokumentasi di publik, Anda perlu menganalisis perilaku aplikasi secara manual untuk menyusun eksploitasi yang sesuai.',
